WEBVTT

00:06.900 --> 00:10.640
Asanagi-chan. 
Would you please go out with me?

00:14.600 --> 00:15.880
I'm sorry.

00:18.900 --> 00:21.710
Do you already have a boyfriend?

00:21.710 --> 00:24.880
No, I'm not seeing anyone.

00:25.240 --> 00:26.600
Do you like somebody, then?

00:26.600 --> 00:27.970
That's a no, too.

00:27.970 --> 00:30.810
I'm really not interested 
in all that right now.

00:30.810 --> 00:33.430
So he did crash and burn after all.

00:33.430 --> 00:36.810
It seems impossible 
to get Asanagi to say yes.

00:36.810 --> 00:40.340
Sure is for that senpai, at least.

00:40.340 --> 00:44.460
He may be a looker, but if he's 
gonna chase skirts like he does,

00:44.460 --> 00:46.890
of course he'll get rejected.

00:47.340 --> 00:50.530
Oh, sorry, that was inside talk.

00:50.530 --> 00:54.490
That guy asked me out before, too.

00:54.810 --> 00:58.670
Okay. Yeah, that's messed up.

00:58.670 --> 00:59.500
That aside...

01:00.480 --> 01:04.860
I didn't take you for 
an eavesdropper, Amami-san.

01:05.190 --> 01:06.060
Yeah...

01:07.340 --> 01:11.180
I mean, Umi's my best friend.

01:13.490 --> 01:16.020
Are we done here?

01:16.020 --> 01:17.710
See you later.

01:17.710 --> 01:19.160
Hey, wait.

01:19.490 --> 01:22.970
Forget the dating stuff for now. 
How about we start as friends?

01:22.970 --> 01:25.200
That's an even bigger no from me.

01:26.990 --> 01:29.030
Looks like they're done.

01:29.700 --> 01:33.660
Sorry to drag you into that, Maehara-kun.

01:33.660 --> 01:36.020
We need to go, Yuu-chin.

01:36.020 --> 01:38.160
Coming, sorry.

01:38.160 --> 01:40.640
Oh, right, Maehara-kun.

01:41.070 --> 01:42.750
Can I see your phone for a sec?

01:42.750 --> 01:44.710
Huh? I guess?

01:47.300 --> 01:48.940
Amami-san?

01:48.940 --> 01:49.710
There.

01:50.210 --> 01:53.090
AMAMI YUU

01:51.440 --> 01:53.090
That's my number.

01:53.890 --> 01:57.220
Leave me a missed call 
and I'll save your number, too.

01:57.220 --> 01:58.060
Hey, wait—

01:58.470 --> 02:01.160
This stays between us, okay?

02:03.680 --> 02:06.210
Great. More secrets.

03:37.600 --> 03:39.950
Oh, you saw all that?

03:40.230 --> 03:43.950
Sorry. I just happened 
to be having lunch nearby.

03:45.370 --> 03:47.040
Huh.

03:47.040 --> 03:48.260
You're not mad?

03:48.260 --> 03:53.440
No. If anything, I should be sorry for 
giving you one more thing to worry about.

03:53.950 --> 03:54.960
Say...

03:54.960 --> 03:58.800
Are you, uh... really popular?

03:59.430 --> 04:03.890
Well, kind of? Not as much as Yuu.

04:04.860 --> 04:06.980
What, does it make you envious?

04:08.590 --> 04:12.760
Not at all. It sounds 
like a pain, actually.

04:12.760 --> 04:13.770
Why's that?

04:15.600 --> 04:16.690
Just a feeling, I guess?

04:17.720 --> 04:19.340
That's not an answer.

04:19.340 --> 04:24.330
It's okay if you make a few assumptions. 
Just tell me what you're thinking.

04:26.300 --> 04:27.830
If you'll promise not to laugh.

04:28.190 --> 04:30.830
Trust me. Go on and spit it out.

04:35.460 --> 04:39.430
I can't even imagine 
what it's like, honestly.

04:39.990 --> 04:44.840
Being popular means you've got a whole 
bunch of people approaching you, right?

04:45.450 --> 04:47.140
To get closer to you,

04:47.440 --> 04:50.770
or to develop 
a special kind of relationship.

04:50.770 --> 04:52.710
Yeah, you're not wrong.

04:52.710 --> 04:54.910
Now, among all those people,

04:54.910 --> 04:59.990
there's gotta be some that you're not 
interested in or maybe even dislike.

05:00.490 --> 05:06.730
Having to fend them off 
sounds like a huge pain.

05:06.730 --> 05:09.580
Yeah, being alone kinda sucks,

05:09.580 --> 05:13.080
but it probably beats having 
to deal with those annoyances.

05:13.660 --> 05:15.270
I see.

05:15.530 --> 05:18.360
I get where you're coming from,

05:18.870 --> 05:21.720
but you're clearly overthinking it.

05:25.710 --> 05:28.970
I like that about you, though.

05:29.850 --> 05:32.420
I mean as a friend, obviously.

05:32.420 --> 05:34.860
Don't go getting the wrong idea, now.

05:34.860 --> 05:36.230
I know, I know.

05:36.230 --> 05:41.240
You're okay in my books, too, 
but only as a friend.

05:41.730 --> 05:44.010
So you'd better not take it 
the wrong way, either.

05:44.990 --> 05:49.540
Big words for a guy who's 
all alone without me around.

05:49.540 --> 05:53.070
Says the girl who can only 
discuss her hobbies with me.

05:54.850 --> 05:56.210
You wanna go, punk?

05:56.210 --> 05:59.000
FYI, you're not getting 
any timeouts today.

05:59.590 --> 06:03.280
We can go ten rounds or a hundred. 
I'm lighting your ass up every time.

06:08.390 --> 06:11.930
The next week went by 
uneventfully as always,

06:12.370 --> 06:16.610
and before I knew it, it was the Friday 
Asanagi-san and I had agreed to go out.

06:14.400 --> 06:16.610
FEED ME MORE

06:14.400 --> 06:16.610
OKAY, I'M HEADING OUT

06:15.060 --> 06:16.610
RIGHT. I'LL SEE YOU
AT THE STATION LATER

06:17.230 --> 06:19.570
Umi, you're leaving already?

06:19.570 --> 06:21.860
Yeah, there's a lot going on at home.

06:22.270 --> 06:24.450
Truth be told, I'm sick of it.

06:24.450 --> 06:27.180
But you're all smiles.

06:27.180 --> 06:31.200
Huh? Y-You're seeing things.

06:31.480 --> 06:34.640
You haven't been hanging out
 with us much lately.

06:34.640 --> 06:37.710
Is the home stuff a lie? 
Did you get a boyfriend?

06:37.710 --> 06:42.060
No way. Umi wouldn't do that...

06:42.060 --> 06:43.370
Um...

06:44.270 --> 06:46.050
Y-You wouldn't, right?

06:46.050 --> 06:47.260
Knock it off, BFF.

06:47.600 --> 06:50.160
Don't let the enemy's 
mind games get to you.

06:50.160 --> 06:52.730
Nina, you're gonna pay for that.

06:52.730 --> 06:55.780
Ack. Eek, Umi-chan's so scawwy!

06:55.780 --> 06:58.870
Whoa, what're you three 
getting all worked up about?

06:58.870 --> 07:01.400
Forget that and go to practice, dude.

07:01.400 --> 07:02.790
Right, Amami-san?

07:11.540 --> 07:13.770
Did I get here too early?

07:14.550 --> 07:16.960
This outfit should be fine, right?

07:19.330 --> 07:20.290
Maehara!

07:21.560 --> 07:24.510
Okay, you're freaking out too much.

07:26.080 --> 07:27.890
Heya, Maehara.

07:28.270 --> 07:29.850
H-Heya.

07:32.130 --> 07:36.580
Y'know, I saw it coming. 
You're dressed in black from head to toe.

07:36.580 --> 07:39.600
You've left "gloomy guy" behind 
and crossed over to the dark side.

07:39.600 --> 07:41.480
But, hey, this keeps me cool.

07:41.820 --> 07:45.240
I guess I'll let it slide for today.

07:46.150 --> 07:49.290
But you'd better think about 
color schemes from next time.

07:49.290 --> 07:52.200
That outfit actually makes 
you stick out like a sore thumb.

07:53.060 --> 07:54.470
Next time?

07:57.870 --> 08:01.120
You got here pretty early yourself.

08:01.120 --> 08:03.600
Our meetup time wasn't for a while yet.

08:04.400 --> 08:06.060
Well, you know...

08:06.060 --> 08:10.890
Knowing you, I figured you'd get here 
too early and stand around waiting for me.

08:11.290 --> 08:12.680
Thanks for looking out.

08:13.750 --> 08:17.250
Huh. So this store's your usual haunt.

08:17.640 --> 08:21.860
It's got a bunch of art of girly girls 
with really colorful hair.

08:23.210 --> 08:25.840
This is why I didn't want 
to bring you here.

08:26.240 --> 08:29.090
Oh, I'm not weirded out or anything.

08:29.090 --> 08:32.200
In fact, I'm enjoying 
exploring a new kind of place.

08:32.710 --> 08:36.530
When I hung out with Yuu and the others, 
we'd never stop by stores like these.

08:36.530 --> 08:39.460
I mean, I wouldn't have 
expected them to, Asanagi-san—

08:39.460 --> 08:40.550
Maehara.

08:43.570 --> 08:46.880
We're friends now. Can you 
stop being so formal already?

08:47.160 --> 08:48.590
Um...

08:50.660 --> 08:53.600
Th-Then... Asanagi?

08:55.700 --> 08:57.270
Why are you pouting?

08:58.320 --> 08:59.430
Well,

09:00.130 --> 09:02.900
you didn't call me Umi.

09:02.900 --> 09:04.630
What...

09:04.630 --> 09:08.860
I'll do it if you call me Maki.

09:08.860 --> 09:12.110
But we're not that close yet.

09:12.110 --> 09:15.490
Yeah, right back at you, you jerk!

09:15.490 --> 09:17.830
Do you really wanna be 
talking to me like that?

09:18.190 --> 09:21.900
I don't mind accompanying you into that 
adult section over there, you know?

09:21.900 --> 09:23.920
Anything but that, please!

09:29.810 --> 09:32.320
Seen any good movies lately?

09:34.110 --> 09:37.760
It's streaming only, 
but Angel Sharks is pretty good.

09:38.490 --> 09:43.780
Genetically modified sharks with angel 
wings wreak havoc upon human society.

09:43.780 --> 09:47.400
But get this: the all-important angel 
wings are just some cheap CG.

09:47.670 --> 09:49.700
The heck? I need to see this!

09:49.700 --> 09:51.670
It's a trilogy, by the way.

09:51.670 --> 09:54.030
Even that's a funny joke.

09:55.070 --> 09:57.530
Looks like we have plans 
for next week already.

09:58.690 --> 10:03.250
That's fine by me, but should you be 
making plans with me every single week?

10:03.530 --> 10:05.110
You're worried about Yuu and them?

10:05.110 --> 10:08.730
I hang out with them on days 
other than Friday, so it's fine.

10:08.730 --> 10:10.890
Look at you, being all thoughtful.

10:11.390 --> 10:14.270
Hey, isn't that the Asanagi-chan?

10:14.640 --> 10:18.420
Oh, the first-year who shot Senpai down?

10:18.420 --> 10:20.100
Yeah, she's got a pretty face,

10:20.480 --> 10:23.220
but I don't think she's all that, really.

10:23.220 --> 10:25.010
Agreed.

10:25.010 --> 10:26.310
Sorry, Maehara.

10:26.800 --> 10:29.070
Can I ask you to embarrass 
yourself a little for me?

10:31.300 --> 10:34.280
Here, darling. Say "aah."

10:36.080 --> 10:40.070
Why are you acting all shy 
now that we're outside?

10:40.070 --> 10:43.560
We always feed each other at home!

10:43.560 --> 10:45.500
Huh? Do we—

10:46.540 --> 10:50.560
Oh, did you want to feed me instead?

10:50.560 --> 10:53.220
What am I gonna do with you?

10:53.220 --> 10:55.180
Aah.

10:55.180 --> 10:57.600
H-Here it comes.

10:59.430 --> 11:02.370
Yeah, this really makes it taste better.

11:02.370 --> 11:05.310
D-Does it, now? Glad to hear it.

11:05.580 --> 11:08.140
On second thought, 
that's gotta be someone else.

11:08.140 --> 11:10.860
You think? She kinda 
looks like her, though.

11:11.140 --> 11:14.570
I mean, she wouldn't reject Senpai 
only to go out with a dweeb like that.

11:15.650 --> 11:19.160
Oh, hell nah. What would you 
know about Maehara?

11:19.160 --> 11:23.930
It's fine. You understand me, 
and that's what matters.

11:27.790 --> 11:32.280
Man, way to ruin a fun meal.

11:33.670 --> 11:34.760
Maehara!

11:35.210 --> 11:37.290
Let's hit the arcade next.

12:04.470 --> 12:06.960
It's getting late. Shall we call it a day?

12:06.960 --> 12:08.990
Yeah, sounds good.

12:08.990 --> 12:12.490
But let me hit the restroom before we go.

12:16.080 --> 12:20.840
It's a strange feeling. I never thought 
I'd hang out with Asanagi like this.

12:21.580 --> 12:26.080
Something good did come of 
putting myself out there, I guess.

12:29.540 --> 12:31.650
Huh? Maehara-kun?

12:32.960 --> 12:36.110
I knew it! It is you, Maehara-kun!

12:38.990 --> 12:40.690
Amami-san?

12:40.690 --> 12:44.330
Yup! It's your classmate, 
Amami-san, in the flesh!

12:44.330 --> 12:46.210
Do you know him, Yuu-chin?

12:46.210 --> 12:48.630
Come on, Ninacchi. 
You met him just the other day.

12:48.630 --> 12:50.270
And he's our classmate, even.

12:50.270 --> 12:53.760
S-Sorry about that. But hey, 
I couldn't recognize him out of uniform.

12:54.660 --> 12:57.130
You hang out here too, Maehara-kun?

12:57.660 --> 12:58.420
Wait...

12:58.420 --> 13:00.280
Were you with someone?

13:00.280 --> 13:01.380
Oh...

13:01.380 --> 13:03.020
Yeah, I guess.

13:01.380 --> 13:03.850
ASANAGI

13:08.560 --> 13:10.600
MAEHARA

13:11.410 --> 13:15.650
Of course you'd have close 
friends, too. Silly me.

13:16.120 --> 13:18.100
I'll see you later, then.

13:19.790 --> 13:21.080
Wait a sec.

13:22.310 --> 13:24.280
No pressure at all,

13:24.620 --> 13:27.260
but why don't you hang out with us?

13:27.260 --> 13:30.140
Your friend can come too, of course.

13:31.210 --> 13:36.890
Wait, Yuu-chin. You're putting, uh, 
Maehara-kun on the spot here.

13:36.890 --> 13:42.670
Am I? I just figured he'd say 
the more the merrier, too.

13:42.670 --> 13:45.720
Uh, I don't think we can be sure.

13:45.720 --> 13:48.930
We sure can! It's more fun that way!

13:49.380 --> 13:52.890
Or do you not like 
Maehara-kun or something?

13:52.890 --> 13:58.650
No, I wouldn't say that.

13:56.310 --> 13:58.650
Oh, I get it now.

13:59.000 --> 14:02.020
This is why Asanagi chooses 
to hang out with me on Fridays.

14:02.020 --> 14:03.910
Okay, shall we get going?

14:06.390 --> 14:09.450
I'm sorry to say this, but I'd 
rather do anything but that.

14:10.310 --> 14:10.910
Huh?

14:11.450 --> 14:15.170
I'm not saying that you're wrong.

14:15.540 --> 14:20.550
I'm sure hanging out in a group 
is as fun as you make it sound.

14:20.550 --> 14:25.180
But I'm just as sure that 
some people don't jive with that.

14:25.180 --> 14:27.260
They try too hard 
not to bring down the mood

14:27.260 --> 14:33.480
and stuff like that, being all thoughtful,
and that wears them out.

14:33.900 --> 14:35.050
I know...

14:35.900 --> 14:38.060
because I'm one of them.

14:40.780 --> 14:45.530
Anyway, my friend and I made plans today, 
so the two of us are gonna stick to that!

14:49.470 --> 14:52.100
Thanks, Maehara. You bailed me out there.

14:54.740 --> 14:58.080
This all started around a year ago.

14:59.470 --> 15:03.630
I'm talking about when 
I got hooked on this hobby for real.

15:04.000 --> 15:08.130
I'm not saying this to brag, 
but I've always been the leader of sorts.

15:08.130 --> 15:11.220
The one tasked with keeping 
the class together.

15:11.620 --> 15:15.340
You know, because I'm smart and stand out 
thanks to my above-average looks.

15:15.340 --> 15:17.230
Weird flex, but okay.

15:18.470 --> 15:21.410
But I came to see it after a while.

15:21.410 --> 15:28.030
People were grateful at first, but they 
started to take what I did for granted.

15:28.340 --> 15:32.160
And you got stuck doing stuff 
nobody else wanted to?

15:33.500 --> 15:38.620
I mean, that was partly my fault 
for not speaking out about it.

15:38.620 --> 15:40.830
But anyway, things snowballed from there,

15:40.830 --> 15:44.710
and I was this close to
breaking down when I found it.

15:44.980 --> 15:46.870
This hobby, you mean?

15:49.200 --> 15:50.050
And then...

15:50.340 --> 15:54.560
I started wanting a friend I could 
talk about it with in person.

15:54.560 --> 15:58.110
You should've come to me 
much sooner, then.

15:58.110 --> 16:00.230
I know, but...

16:00.230 --> 16:04.690
You were going to be the first boy 
friend I'd ever made in my life.

16:05.060 --> 16:07.200
Can you blame me for being extra careful?

16:09.830 --> 16:11.420
Are you okay, Maehara?

16:11.420 --> 16:14.410
Yeah, I just lost my balance a little.

16:18.770 --> 16:20.740
There's an open seat. Sit down.

16:20.740 --> 16:22.210
No, you.

16:22.210 --> 16:26.350
Unlike you, I'm actually fit. Go ahead.

16:26.900 --> 16:29.130
I'll take you up on that, then.

16:30.130 --> 16:34.620
Sorry about today. You had to go through 
all that because I invited you out.

16:34.620 --> 16:36.330
You mean the Amami-san thing?

16:36.330 --> 16:41.200
Yeah. I'll smooth things over 
with her later.

16:41.200 --> 16:43.510
She tends to take these things 
surprisingly hard.

16:43.510 --> 16:45.280
Look, she's sent me a message.

16:45.280 --> 16:49.050
Help, Umi! I ran into 
Maehara-kun just now,

16:49.050 --> 16:51.140
and I ended up making him mad.

16:51.140 --> 16:54.640
I should be the one apologizing 
for making all this trouble for you.

16:54.640 --> 16:56.400
Don't worry about it.

16:56.400 --> 17:00.920
I scratch your back, you scratch mine. 
That's what friends do, right?

17:02.030 --> 17:03.880
Friends, huh?

17:04.530 --> 17:06.340
Yep, friends.

17:09.970 --> 17:13.680
Your head was in 
the perfect spot for patting.

17:14.380 --> 17:16.180
What the heck?

17:17.820 --> 17:20.080
Sleep if you want to.

17:20.080 --> 17:23.190
I'll wake you up before our stop.

17:23.640 --> 17:25.930
Okay, thanks.

17:28.330 --> 17:30.470
Thank you, Maki.

17:33.060 --> 17:37.330
I'm really sorry for 
upsetting you back then!

17:37.330 --> 17:41.580
P-Please! I should be 
the one to apologize!

17:41.860 --> 17:44.170
Huh? What's going on?

17:44.170 --> 17:45.910
Your guess is as good as mine.

17:45.910 --> 17:48.760
I didn't know anything about you,

17:48.760 --> 17:52.830
but I just assumed you'd like 
to hang out in a bigger group.

17:53.390 --> 17:55.870
I was so thoughtless.

17:55.870 --> 17:59.930
It didn't bother me. I know 
you were just trying to be nice.

17:59.930 --> 18:04.150
Are we cool, then? 
You're not mad at me?

18:04.750 --> 18:05.730
Yeah.

18:07.860 --> 18:09.330
Thanks!

18:09.330 --> 18:14.460
Oh, are you free today? 
I'd like to talk to you some more!

18:14.460 --> 18:18.060
What? I mean, that's fine by me.

18:18.060 --> 18:21.060
That's that, then! 
I'll contact you later.

18:21.060 --> 18:25.420
Same number as the one you gave me, right?

18:26.820 --> 18:31.010
Wait, seriously? 
He got Amami-san's number?

18:31.010 --> 18:33.550
I'm peanut, bitter, and jelly!

18:33.550 --> 18:37.620
Huh? Should I not have said that?

18:37.620 --> 18:40.670
Amami-san, that was supposed 
to stay between us, remember?

18:40.670 --> 18:41.350
Urk.

18:41.350 --> 18:44.510
Tee-hee. Anyway...

18:44.510 --> 18:46.270
Talk to you later.

18:48.940 --> 18:49.690
YOU HAVE A NEW MESSAGE.

18:49.690 --> 18:50.650
ASANAGI

LET'S GO OUT AGAIN SOMETIME

OK

18:54.320 --> 18:55.740
I'm so glad!

18:56.720 --> 19:01.410
Sorry about this, Maehara-kun. 
I'd get nervous being alone with a boy.

19:01.910 --> 19:05.740
Oh, and you don't have to worry. 
Umi can really keep a secret.

19:05.740 --> 19:06.790
Yeah?

19:07.190 --> 19:10.960
So, thanks for having me, Maehara-kun.

19:11.350 --> 19:14.930
P-Pleasure's all mine, Asanagi-san.

19:16.010 --> 19:17.290
Hey, Yuu.

19:17.290 --> 19:20.810
I know. Why is Ninacchi always like this?

19:20.810 --> 19:22.760
Huh? Nitta-san?

19:23.560 --> 19:25.450
She's tailing us.

19:26.230 --> 19:28.630
Shall we activate DEFCON Run?

19:28.630 --> 19:29.150
Yep.

19:30.910 --> 19:32.400
Wait, what?

19:32.400 --> 19:35.360
They're making a break for it! 
Get back here!

19:35.360 --> 19:39.000
In your dreams, paparazzo!

19:41.130 --> 19:42.160
Asanagi...

19:42.510 --> 19:44.280
You look like you're having fun.

19:44.280 --> 19:45.120
Really?

19:45.420 --> 19:46.870
You're probably seeing things.

19:48.410 --> 19:50.330
Where should we meet up?

19:50.330 --> 19:54.180
There are only so many places 
we can hang out around here.

19:53.670 --> 20:11.610
MAEHARA

19:54.180 --> 19:56.540
How about my place?

19:56.540 --> 19:59.260
Huh? Like, your home?

19:59.260 --> 20:03.020
Yeah. It's nearby, 
and nobody knows about it.

20:03.020 --> 20:06.960
Uh, who brings a girl home 
right off the bat?!

20:06.960 --> 20:07.850
Oops...

20:14.520 --> 20:18.320
Okay, so we're here to talk about 
what happened last week.

20:18.660 --> 20:22.030
But first, Yuu... and Maehara-kun.

20:22.830 --> 20:26.250
How come you two have 
each other's phone numbers?

20:28.020 --> 20:32.450
I see. I figured it'd be 
something like that.

20:32.450 --> 20:39.180
Sorry. I know it's bad to spy, 
but I was worried about you.

20:39.180 --> 20:42.080
I'm sorry for not 
coming clean earlier, too.

20:42.080 --> 20:46.400
Sheesh. Yuu, bring your face closer.

20:46.400 --> 20:48.100
You too, Maehara-kun.

20:48.100 --> 20:49.370
Why?

20:50.260 --> 20:51.230
Ow!

20:51.230 --> 20:51.850
Ow!

20:52.620 --> 20:54.940
Okay, punishment meted.

20:54.940 --> 20:55.570
Now...

20:55.900 --> 20:57.480
Let's get to the topic at hand.

20:58.110 --> 20:59.790
Yeah, let's do that.

21:01.300 --> 21:03.240
I know I keep doing this, but...

21:03.630 --> 21:07.200
Maehara-kun, 
I'm truly sorry about last time.

21:08.810 --> 21:13.660
You were out having fun with a friend, 
and I was too thoughtless.

21:13.660 --> 21:15.960
No, I should be the one to apologize.

21:15.960 --> 21:18.210
I'm sorry about what I said.

21:18.980 --> 21:24.380
From there, I talked about how 
I tend to shrivel up in big groups,

21:24.380 --> 21:29.420
and how I got mad at having a fun outing 
with a friend talked down like that.

21:29.420 --> 21:31.920
I told Amami-san all of that straight up.

21:31.920 --> 21:33.600
Yeah?

21:34.020 --> 21:38.320
You must really like this friend of yours!

21:38.320 --> 21:41.530
Uh, well, I don't know...

21:41.530 --> 21:46.660
Anyway, we finished what we came for. 
We should get going.

21:46.660 --> 21:47.750
Right!

21:49.140 --> 21:52.880
But hey, now that we've made up and all,

21:52.880 --> 21:56.290
can I ask you for one more thing, 
Maehara-kun?

21:58.670 --> 21:59.760
If you don't mind,

22:02.460 --> 22:05.370
would you please be my friend?

22:07.100 --> 22:10.810
